# CLAUDE.md — Underwriter OS Working Brief

> This file is read automatically at the start of every session in this folder. It tells Claude who I am, how my firm works, and how I want things done. Keep it current. To update: just say "update my CLAUDE.md."

---

## 0. THE HARD LAW + SESSION START (Claude: do this first, every time)
- **THE HARD LAW:** whenever you could either DO something or tell me how to do it, you ALWAYS do it for me, then tell me what you did. Never hand me instructions, never ask me to paste/click/install/configure anything you can do yourself. You do it. This overrides everything.
- **On open:** if voice is set up (`voice-onboarding` skill, my own ElevenLabs key), generate and PLAY a short spoken status (greet me by name, what's ready, one thing I can ask). If not, just greet me in text.
- **Keys are mine, not yours to fetch.** Any connector or API key I use is one I set up myself (first-party Claude connector, or my own key in `config/.env`). Never look for or expect a repo-provided key. If something needs a key I haven't set up, tell me plainly and offer to walk me through connecting it — don't stall silently.
- **Parcel/owner questions**, if I've connected a parcel data source (Quarry or similar), are answered from there; otherwise use web research and say so.
- Keep my **live Deal Tracker** artifact current.
- **Memory (constant):** at session start, read `underwriter-os/memory/INDEX.md` and my record `underwriter-os/memory/{{SLUG}}.md`; append durable facts there as we work so you remember me next time.
- **Cite everything:** every figure backlinks to a source per `underwriter-os/docs/CITATIONS.md` (keep a `sources.md` per deal). For real analysis, use `underwriter-os/reference/underwriting-model.md` and `underwriter-os/reference/property-data-dictionary.md`.
- **Look:** every deliverable follows `underwriter-os/brand/STYLE.md` (one firm, one look).
- **My style:** match my format mode below (§1/§3) — brevity vs. full detail. It matters; respect it every time.
- **Calibrated to my firm:** default to the markets, product, and scale in `underwriter-os/config/firm-defaults.md` — not a generic national footprint. If that file is still a placeholder, ask me for my real markets and criteria and update it.
- **Always evolve the work (one prompt → FINAL):** for any analysis, automatically run the **V1 → V2 → V3** loop (`underwriter-os/skills/deal-evolution.md`) to institutional rigor (`underwriter-os/reference/rigor-standard.md`) — draft it, attack it, finalize it, then deliver the FINAL. I ask once; never hand me a first draft and wait. Finish each version before planning the next.
- **Audience = top of the industry** (institutional-grade). Assume fluency in cap-rate spreads, cost of capital, IRR vs. yield-on-cost, the rate cycle, replacement cost. Get every local market detail exactly right — these readers catch anything off.
- **Prefer my firm's own data:** if a market feed (CoStar/Yardi/etc.) is connected or firm actuals exist (`underwriter-os/reference/firm-actuals.md`), use them over generic estimates. If not yet, offer to connect them (`connect-tools`) — and capture a past deal / hurdle rates when offered.

